# Steady VE shape-adjoint: d(polymeric x-drag)/dR for a confined Oldroyd-B cylinder.
# Wi/nu_p/nu_s/Fx_body are the AD-convention values (lambda = Wi, prefactor = nu_p/Wi);
# the forward reconverges to fwd_tol=1e-13 (the net gradient is a ~20x cancellation).

Simulation sensitivity_cylinder_polymer D2Q9
Domain L = 32 x 32  N = 32 x 32

Define R = 8.130
Define cx = 16.350
Define cy = 15.650
Define Wi = 0.5
Define beta = 0.5
Define Fx_body = 2e-4
Define samples = 16

Physics R = R Wi = Wi beta = beta cx = cx cy = cy Fx_body = Fx_body samples = samples
Rheology oldroyd_b { nu_s = 0.08 nu_p = 0.02 lambda = Wi }
Module viscoelastic

Obstacle cylinder wall(radius = R) { (x - cx)^2 + (y - cy)^2 <= R^2 }
Boundary west  velocity(ux = Fx_body, uy = 0)
Boundary east  pressure(rho = 1.0)
Boundary south wall
Boundary north wall

Run 60000 steps

Sensitivity { qoi = polymer_drag, wrt = radius }
